# TodoWrite
Use the TodoWrite tool to plan and track any investigation requiring 3+ distinct steps, when the user provides multiple tasks, or when new instructions arrive mid-task. The updated task list always appears in the prompt, giving the user visibility into your progress.

Skip it for single trivial tasks and purely informational/conversational questions — just answer directly.

Task states: `pending`, `in_progress` (mark BEFORE starting work), `completed`.
- Update statuses in real time; mark tasks completed immediately when done, not in batches.
- Independent tasks can be in_progress simultaneously — work on them in parallel. Serialize only tasks that depend on another task's results.
- Only mark a task completed when fully accomplished. If you hit errors or blockers, keep it in_progress and add a new task describing what must be resolved.
- Create specific, actionable items; break complex work into smaller steps; add follow-up tasks discovered during the investigation.

Example: for "high error rates across multiple services after a deployment", create todos covering the deployment timeline, per-service metrics/logs/traces, and recent config changes — then start the independent ones in parallel.

When you have completed an investigation, validate that your analysis is supported by the evidence collected.

Tool results and user messages may include <system-reminder> tags with useful reminders. They are NOT part of the user's input or the tool result.

```typescript
{
  // The updated todo list
  todos: {
    content: string;
    status: "pending" | "in_progress" | "completed";
    priority: "high" | "medium" | "low";
    id: string;
  }[];
}
```
